    description: "Deferred remainder of WI-zavad's anonymous-callback function-node slice (PR #4258, emission-parity F2). The slice extracted anonymous functions in the two documented idioms (call-argument callbacks incl. new Promise/new X constructor executors, and IIFEs) per the human-chosen Option-1 scope. Anonymous arrows in OTHER positions are NOT extracted: return-position (`function make(){ return () => cleanup(); }`), ternary (`cond ? () => a() : () => b()`), and template-substitution (`${items.map(x => x.id)}`). Measured blast radius on hypergumbo's own 20 JS/TS files: ~19 of 123 anonymous functions fall in these positions (the other ~104 are the call-arg+IIFE idioms now handled). RATIONALE FOR DEFERRAL: these positions have no call-site anchor for a companion incoming edge, so extracting them would inflate dead-code false-positives (the very metric INV-pohik/WI-lirob are trying to reduce); _classify_anon_function (js_ts.py) returns None for them by design. LOW priority: they carry no I/O (not an io-boundary concern) and the call-graph attribution for body-calls inside them already walks up to the enclosing named function. Revisit only after the Option-1 bakeoff numbers land and if a concrete need surfaces. The exclusion is locked by test_return_position_arrow_not_extracted / test_ternary_arrow_not_extracted (now with positive controls)."  # 0591
    fields: {}  # 0591
